From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 09:02:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] thermal: qcom: tsens: Mask critical IRQs without a thermal zone

TSENS v2 critical IRQs share a level-triggered line on IPQ9574. The
critical handler skips sensors for which Linux could not register a
thermal zone. If firmware left one of those IRQs unmasked, its pending
status can retrigger the IRQ continuously.

Mask and clear the critical IRQ for these sensors before installing the
handler. Leave all interrupts and trip programming of registered thermal
zones and the TSENS watchdog handling unchanged.

Link: https://github.com/VIKINGYFY/immortalwrt/issues/229
Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/drivers/thermal/qcom/tsens.c
+++ b/drivers/thermal/qcom/tsens.c
@@ -1295,8 +1295,14 @@ static int tsens_register(struct tsens_p
 		tzd = devm_thermal_of_zone_register(priv->dev, priv->sensor[i].hw_id,
 						    &priv->sensor[i],
 						    &tsens_of_ops);
-		if (IS_ERR(tzd))
+		if (IS_ERR(tzd)) {
+			/* The handler cannot service sensors without a zone. */
+			if (priv->feat->crit_int &&
+			    tsens_version(priv) >= VER_2_X)
+				tsens_set_interrupt(priv, priv->sensor[i].hw_id,
+						    CRITICAL, false);
 			continue;
+		}
 		priv->sensor[i].tzd = tzd;
 		if (priv->ops->enable)
 			priv->ops->enable(priv, i);
